What the branch does

1. The PST class is split up. PST<Element> (pst.hpp) is now an abstract base holding the root, hashes and signing, with a pure-virtual hasErrors(). Parsing moved to the new ParsedPST<Element> (parsed_pst.hpp), which picks the parser per call (fromContents<Parser>). There is also a new TemplateExpansionPST (template_expansion_pst.hpp) for subtrees built without parsing. PSTs are now heap-allocated and returned as Box<…>. Most of the diff is call sites switching from . to ->.
2. Element constructors no longer need the parser state. They take LangParserElementConstructionData (source position plus context hash) instead of const LangParserState&. This is the one-line change in ~70 hierarchy headers.
3. Synthetic elements: two new element types, TemplateTopLevel and TemplateExpansionAssignment, built by ElementSynthesizer. The child-assignment logic moved out of PSTAutomatic into a new FreeAutomatic so the synthesizer can use it too.

